{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact sprint-report head e4f3c5cb0cc82038ba97063acedb5db3e91e07e2 on planner/sprint-report-20261102, notes/reports/2026-11-02-sprint-report.md, under promise 3f8e2406 and review request 0123a3eb. Most of the report holds. Two claims are wrong, one is out of date, and one sentence reads two ways.\n\nWhat holds. Main 8e9f0942 is an ancestor. The head adds one path, and the commit-message check passes. Nineteen first-parent landings sit on main from 4acd79c5 at 17:11 on 1 November through 8e9f0942. The three Workers took six deployments: d56394da at 18:00, 31384059 at 21:00, 8093f9ce at 23:00, f277867f at 03:30, 04f4af48 at 08:01 and bcf88654 at 12:54. Every cited ID exists in the workroom or on main and says what the report says. The first-press figures match notes/implementation/2026-11-02-first-press.md: 12 requests became four, and the three before-act times of 4,497, 1,779 and 1,336 ms became 699, 308 and 288 ms. bridge.ts accepts only 2026-01-26. docs/self-host.md:457-459 states that the App key can mint tokens for all 26 repositories. The G3 source note records four full gates, three of them failed. The hosted-cards subject is 111 characters. The survey gap and the refused install match 6a86db9c and dab39a02.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. \"The register installed three minutes into its fourteen-minute window.\" The window's own timeline, ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-02-g3-mini-window/timeline.txt, shows the plan ending at 15:01:41 and the install succeeding at 15:02:44. That is about one minute. Write \"about one minute\".\n\n2. \"The binding row goes to review next.\" I approved the binding row at 488f8e8b as e455a2b9 at 15:34, and this head was committed at 15:37. Say that the checker approved it. If it lands before this report, say that it landed, with its commit.\n\n3. In the cost review, the second G3 gate did not fail on catalog goldens. Per notes/implementation/2026-11-02-repository-binding.md, it failed five plain cases. The catalog lacked four new digest literals, two fixtures expected the old values, and the Page module needed a rebuild. The note also says that all 88 historical goldens stayed exact. Write \"catalog digest literals\" or \"catalog literals and two fixtures\".\n\n4. \"The wait fell from 1.3 to 4.5 seconds to under 0.7 seconds\" first reads as a rise from 1.3 to 4.5. Write \"fell from between 1.3 and 4.5 seconds to under 0.7 seconds\".\n\nNot required. The decision line for 9cf4b1cd is accurate as far as it goes. My correction e128ebd1 adds that a bind under the old bundle is not a no-op. That belongs in the parent's record, not in this report.\n\nThe report describes only work done, at adopter level, and its stories read in order.\n\nArchitecture: not applicable to a report; no design claim changes. Security: no credential or private value appears. Simplification: no change needed beyond the four above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c84776e682a8cce3ee638585a9d073527930cbc4","binding":"assigned","head":"e4f3c5cb0cc82038ba97063acedb5db3e91e07e2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:04bd8c2268611e018d4df0c3b2d25b1a11fda975\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f8e2406a815c573cee7e6732e354c2ec15727f4\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14f06cb6c44918ce8ff4b4d9d06704504558b22b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}